          <p>
            Be wary of boxes that promise one plug-in heater will warm 500 or 1,000 square feet. At 5,118 BTU per hour that is only possible as a gentle top-up in a space that is already mostly warm. If the room is too big for one 1,500-watt heater, there is no "more powerful" plug-in to buy; the answer is two heaters on two different circuits, a hardwired 240-volt heater, or a proper fix such as a mini split. And if your heater runs on high for hours without reaching its set temperature, the room is losing heat faster than 5,118 BTU per hour, and no mode setting will change that.
          </p>
